            <ArticleTitle>Radiation-recall myositis presenting as low-back pain (2010: 4b).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1799-801</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00330-009-1562-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a patient with a history of Ewing sarcoma who underwent surgery and subsequent adjuvant chemotherapy and radiotherapy. He developed low-back pain 6 months after the end of the radiotherapy and during consolidation chemotherapy. Magnetic resonance imaging showed evidence of myositis corresponding to the 'radiation-recall phenomenon', an inflammatory reaction of irradiated tissue.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
